--- original/verification/NFRT-SEED-POLICY.md
+++ repaired/verification/NFRT-SEED-POLICY.md
@@ -9,3 +9,11 @@
 The host mounts the approved seed and manifest read-only; the container validates again, copies bytes into a fresh private intermediate directory, and validates the result. NFRT may update only the private copy. No project output, compilation history, application/test classes, reports or prior acceptance decisions are reused. Downloaded-input validation, fresh project compilation, offline execution and all frozen gates remain in force.
 
 This mechanism does not claim that all Gradle builds or source-only edits have invariant reconstruction inputs. An attestation requires evidence for its particular build and allowed source scope. TRANSITION-004C's approved attestation and supporting measurements are outside production code; production contains no task name or application filename.
+
+## Reviewed source-class attestation (v2)
+
+`hive-nfrt-seed-v2` replaces the file list with a host-pinned `independent_source_policy` of kind `reviewed-main-java-v1`. It permits regular `.java` contents and membership to vary only within explicitly reviewed roots of the measured **main** Java source set. Every other source/config file and its membership remains fixed. Test sources, resources, build scripts, properties, mappings, transform/injection data, dependency coordinates and unknown additions remain invalidations. The v1 format retains its original semantics; mixed policies are rejected.
+
+Approval requires pinned implementation/build review demonstrating that reconstruction does not consume the variable source class, in addition to measured input equality. The manifest contains normalized `$PROJECT` reconstruction inputs, the main source roots, a reconstruction task graph without compilation prerequisites, all optional input collections and SHA-256 references to the sealed review/dependency model. The host pins the entire manifest. Input collections overlapping a claimed independent root are rejected, including a Java-named file selected as access-transformer data. Equal declared inputs alone do not authorize a new build with undeclared source reads.
+
+The measured source roots are evidence, not an automatic `src/main/java/**` exemption for arbitrary projects. Fixed build/plugin/tool bytes and the reviewed absent source dependency justify this particular attestation. A different build, tool, option, resource or dependency identity requires a fresh compatibility review. All seed/provenance/module/download hashes, image/JDK and wrapper/profile checks remain in force. Source compatibility says nothing about candidate correctness: main/test compilation and acceptance run fresh, with unchanged rerun/no-build-cache flags and deadlines.
